    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cmdline\n\n### Question\n\nWhen I am navigating the options for completion with mini.cmdline, I'd like to be able to view the documentation for a command, e.g. by pressing `<C-Space>` when hovering an entry in the menu.\r\n\r\nIs it possible?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.cmdline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I am navigating the options for completion with mini.cmdline, I'd like to be able to view the documentation for a command, e.g. by pressing <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-Space&gt;</code> when hovering an entry in the menu.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.cmdline\nQuestion\nWhen I am navigating the options for completion with mini.cmdline, I'd like to be able to view the documentation for a command, e.g. by pressing <C-Space> when hovering an entry in the menu.\nIs it possible?",
