    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2026-06-15T09:07:29Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Autocompletion in 'mini.cmdline' [builds on top of built-in Command-line completion](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/a59a9b7fb0a42cbcf022938ee5f0724320b66f63/doc/mini-cmdline.txt#L155-L156), i.e. `:h 'wildmenu'`. As far as I know, it doesn't support showing command documentation. Even more, there doesn't seem to be a way to automatically get built-in command descriptions. There is an open PR (neovim/neovim#39672), but it would not add the \"documentation window\" to wildmenu.\r\n\r\n> Is it possible?\r\n\r\nSo the answer is \"Not yet, at least until it is a built-in wildmenu feature\".",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Autocompletion in 'mini.cmdline' <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/a59a9b7fb0a42cbcf022938ee5f0724320b66f63/doc/mini-cmdline.txt#L155-L156\">builds on top of built-in Command-line completion</a>, i.e. <code class=\"notranslate\">:h 'wildmenu'</code>. As far as I know, it doesn't support showing command documentation. Even more, there doesn't seem to be a way to automatically get built-in command descriptions. There is an open PR (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4404993162\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39672\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/neovim/neovim/pull/39672/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/39672\">neovim/neovim#39672</a>), but it would not add the \"documentation window\" to wildmenu.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So the answer is \"Not yet, at least until it is a built-in wildmenu feature\".</p>",
            "bodyText": "Autocompletion in 'mini.cmdline' builds on top of built-in Command-line completion, i.e. :h 'wildmenu'. As far as I know, it doesn't support showing command documentation. Even more, there doesn't seem to be a way to automatically get built-in command descriptions. There is an open PR (neovim/neovim#39672), but it would not add the \"documentation window\" to wildmenu.\n\nIs it possible?\n\nSo the answer is \"Not yet, at least until it is a built-in wildmenu feature\".",
